- `element.ref` — in React 19 dev, a getter with a warning? Actually, React 19 dev: `element.ref` is a getter that warns ("Accessing element.ref is deprecated..."? no wait — that's 18). React 19: `element.props.ref` works, and `element.ref` also works but one of them warns depending on version. The snapshot `getElementRef` code:
  ```tsx
  let getter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element.props, 'ref')?.get;
  let mayWarn = getter && 'isReactWarning' in getter && getter.isReactWarning;
  if (mayWarn) return (element as any).ref;  // React <=18 in DEV
  getter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element, 'ref')?.get;
  mayWarn = getter && 'isReactWarning' in getter && getter.isReactWarning;
  if (mayWarn) return (element.props as { ref?: React.Ref<unknown> }).ref;  // React 19 in DEV
